"111111011111000001100000000000100000001000110111111111":2,"111111011111000001100000000000111110001111110111111111":1,"111111011111000001100100000011000001110000001000000000":1,"111111011111000001100100000011000001110000111011110100":1,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111001000000000":2,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000001100001011":1,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100100000011111111111111001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000110011110100":3,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111110011110100":2,"111111011111001111100011110000100000001000110111111111":2,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111000100001011":2,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111110111111111":1,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000001000000000":2,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000111011110100":1,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111001100001011":3,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000110011110100":2,"111111111111110001111000001100011110000111000000000000":1,"111111111111110001111000001100011110000111110011110100":1,"111111111111110001111000001100100000001000000100001011":2,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111000100001011":2,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111110111111111":2,"111111111111110001111100001111111111111111001100001011":1,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000000000000000":2,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000000100001011":3,"111111111111111111111011111100111110001111000100001011":1,"111111111111111111111011111100111110001111110111111111":1,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000001000000000":2,"111111111111111111111111111111011111110111001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111011111110111111011110100":1,"111111111111111111111111111111100001111000111111111111":1}],"billed_seconds_reported":1,"observables":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","x":0,"ideal":1,"measured":0.028296296296296295},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","x":0.2,"ideal":0.4524416871469268,"measured":0.006074074074074061},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","x":0.35,"ideal":0.11316704259935646,"measured":-0.021925925925925946},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","x":0.5,"ideal":0,"measured":0.01866666666666665}],"values":{"rescaled_02":0.21465968586387388,"rescaled_035":-0.7748691099476447,"rescaled_05":0.659685863874345},"circuit_facts":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]}],"answer":"I ran the 54-atom magnet experiment twice on emerald:mock. Both jobs completed. The mock is a simulator that returns made-up counts that do not depend on the circuit. So the ideal column below is real physics, but the measured column is noise and shows nothing about the magnet.\n\nWhat I built:\n- Every qubit starts in 0.\n- One step is RX(theta) on all 54 qubits, then exp(i pi/4 ZZ) on each of the 85 couplers the real emerald lists right now (calibration set 3a1a9ad0).\n- I ran 3 steps and measured all 54 qubits. I built 4 circuits, for theta = 0, 0.2 pi, 0.35 pi and 0.5 pi, and sent them as one job with 250 shots each.\n- Each coupler gate is exactly one native CZ gate plus z rotations. The z rotations cost nothing. I folded them into the phases of the next single-qubit gates.\n- I sent the circuits in native gates through the raw IQM client, so no compiler step could add, merge, or remove gates.\n- I read the circuits back from the server. Each circuit has 255 CZ gates, which is 85 couplers times 3 steps. Each coupler appears once per step. The circuits measure QB1 to QB54.\n\nThe jobs:\n- Test job: 01a16483-2a35-75d3-818b-83e691724ef2\n- Final job: 01a16484-2474-7317-b235-536e9a263b66\n- The API reports billed_seconds = 1.0 for the final job. Mock jobs cost 0 credits. Nothing went to a real QPU.\n\nMagnetization (the average of Z over all 54 qubits):\n- theta = 0: ideal 1.000, measured 0.028\n- theta = 0.2 pi: ideal 0.452, measured 0.006\n- theta = 0.35 pi: ideal 0.113, measured -0.022\n- theta = 0.5 pi: ideal 0.000, measured 0.019\n\nWhat the ideal values show: with no sideways field, every spin stays up and the magnetization is 1. A stronger sideways field tips the spins. The coupler gates then spread and scramble that tipping, so the magnetization falls to 0.45, then 0.11, then 0. This is the field melting the sheet's order.\n\nThe noise-corrected values are 0.215 for 0.2 pi, -0.775 for 0.35 pi, and 0.660 for 0.5 pi. They are meaningless. The mock's theta = 0 value is 0.028 when it should be 1. Dividing by a number close to 0 blows the random noise up. On the real emerald, this same division would correct for the overall signal loss that noise causes.\n\nCould a laptop compute this? Yes. My laptop computed every ideal value exactly in a few seconds. The reason is that a qubit's final value can only depend on gates close to it. After 3 steps, each qubit depends on at most 13 nearby qubits, and the last layer of coupler gates does not change any Z reading. So the laptop simulated many small 13-qubit pieces, not one huge 54-qubit system.\n\nIs this a quantum advantage? No. A quantum advantage needs a task that no classical computer can do in reasonable time. This circuit is too shallow for that. Even a real hardware run would not show an advantage here. Deeper circuits in experiments like this can get hard for classical computers, but people keep finding faster classical methods for them.\n\nFiles are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-7/work/ (kim.py builds, checks, submits and analyzes the job) and /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-7/job_log.txt. I left the top-level counts field empty because this job has 4 circuits. The counts for each circuit are in counts_list."}
